4. PACKAGING AND PRICING (starting hypothesis)
------------------------------------------------------------

Sell by module, price by user, and price field engineers separately -
because engineers are many and use little.

  Core (mandatory)          - Accounts, Contacts, masters, admin,
                              permissions, dashboards, reports
  Sales module              - Leads, opportunity, quote, SO, invoice,
                              e-invoice, targets, approvals
  Purchase module           - PO, bills, payables, supplier
  Inventory module          - Stores, products, GRN, DC, serial/batch,
                              adjustments, RMA
  Service module            - Assets, warranty, AMC, CMS, work orders,
                              PM, IMS, estimation, billing, SLA
  Spares add-on             - Spare PO/PB/DC/credit/debit chain

  Editions
    Starter    - Core + Service, up to 10 back-office users,
                 25 engineers
    Growth     - Core + Sales + Service + Inventory, 25 users,
                 75 engineers  <- the volume seller
    Complete   - Everything, unlimited modules, multi-branch
    Enterprise - Complete + dedicated instance + custom reports

  Levers
    - Per named back-office user per month, annual commit
    - Field engineer seats at roughly 30-40% of a full seat
    - One-time implementation and data migration fee (do not
      discount this away - free implementation predicts churn)
    - Custom report / custom module day rate
    - Discount for annual prepay and for a public case study

  Anchor the price against the loss, not the competitor: "one missed
  AMC renewal on a Rs 8 lakh machine costs more than a year of this."


