5. GO-TO-MARKET
------------------------------------------------------------

5.1 Motion

  This is a Rs 3-15 lakh ACV, 60-120 day, multi-stakeholder,
  demo-led sale into a conservative buyer. That means founder-led
  outbound plus vertical credibility. It is not a self-serve signup
  product and it never will be. Do not build a free-trial funnel.

  Funnel shape to design for
    Vertical content / referral / outbound
      -> ROI calculator or benchmark report (lead magnet)
      -> 30-min discovery call
      -> tailored demo on their vertical's data
      -> 6-week paid pilot, one branch, Service module only
      -> full rollout
      -> module expansion (Sales, Inventory) at month 9-18

  Land on Service. Expand into Sales and Inventory. The service head
  is the champion, the service pain is the sharpest, and the service
  module is the hardest thing for any competitor to match.

5.2 Channels, in priority order

  1. Founder-led outbound to Tier 1 verticals
     Build a list of 300 named companies from: IndiaMART supplier
     lists, medical device distributor directories, machine-tool
     association members (IMTMA), packaging associations, GST
     directories by HSN. Target the Service Head on LinkedIn, not
     the MD. One vertical at a time, one message per vertical.

  2. Vertical trade associations and expos
     IMTMA / IMTEX (machine tools), India Med Expo and medical
     device distributor bodies, PackPlus / printing expos, ACREX
     (HVAC), Elecrama. A 3x3 stall with one screen showing the
     service dashboard on a real installed base outperforms any ad
     spend at this ACV.

  3. OEM referral channel - the highest-leverage play
     A single OEM (say a Japanese or German machine principal) has
     20-60 Indian dealers who all have the same problem. Sell to one
     dealer, get introduced to the OEM's channel management, become
     the recommended dealer system. One OEM relationship can be
     worth 20 customers. Prioritise this above all paid marketing.

  4. Chartered accountant and Tally partner referrals
     They already sit inside the finance function of every target.
     Position explicitly as non-competing with Tally, pay referral
     commission.

  5. LinkedIn ABM
     Target titles: Service Head, National Service Manager, Customer
     Support Head, GM Service, Spare Parts Manager, plus MD/Director
     at the named 300. Content, not ads, at this stage.

  6. Google Search - high-intent long-tail only
     Do not bid on "CRM software" or "ERP software". Bid on
     "AMC management software India", "field service management
     software for medical equipment", "spare parts management
     software dealer", "service CRM with GST e-invoice",
     "ServitiumCRM alternative", "Zoho FSM alternative India".

  7. YouTube product walkthroughs
     Screen-recorded, 6-10 minutes, one workflow each, no music, no
     stock footage. "Complaint to work order to spare indent to
     bill, in 8 minutes." Indian buyers watch these before booking.

  8. Review sites
     Get listed on G2, Capterra, SoftwareSuggest and Techjockey.
     Techjockey and SoftwareSuggest genuinely generate Indian
     mid-market leads. Seed with 5-8 real reviews from Arlikat users.

5.3 First 90 days

  Weeks 1-2
    - Lock the product name, domain, logo, one-line positioning
    - Get written permission for an Arlikat case study
    - Record 5 core demo videos
  Weeks 3-6
    - Ship the website: home, product overview, 5 module pages,
      2 industry pages, pricing, demo booking, about (see section 6)
    - Build the AMC Revenue Leakage Calculator (the flagship lead
      magnet)
    - Publish the Arlikat case study with real numbers
  Weeks 7-10
    - Build the named-300 list for Tier 1 verticals
    - Start outbound; target 40 discovery calls
    - List on Techjockey, SoftwareSuggest, G2, Capterra
    - Publish 4 pillar articles (section 6.6)
  Weeks 11-13
    - First expo or association event booked
    - Approach 3 OEMs for channel introductions
    - Target: 3 paid pilots signed

  Months 4-6: second vertical, 2 more case studies, WhatsApp
  notifications shipped (it removes a recurring objection).
  Months 7-12: customer portal and engineer mobile app shipped,
  partner/reseller programme opened, target 12-15 customers.

5.4 Metrics

  Leading    - named accounts reached, discovery calls booked,
               demos delivered, calculator completions
  Mid-funnel - demo-to-pilot rate (target 30%), pilot-to-paid rate
               (target 60%)
  Lagging    - ACV, CAC payback (target under 12 months), logo
               churn, module expansion revenue, net revenue retention
  Product    - weekly active engineers, work orders closed in-system,
               percentage of AMC renewals captured before expiry.
               That last one is the number that proves the pitch.


